hes, application configuration, and firewall (Security Group) rules","Decommissioning old storage disks and shredding drives","Global undersea fiber-optic cable maintenance"],"question":"Under the AWS Shared Responsibility Model, which of the following is the customer's responsibility when using Amazon EC2?"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Attaching an IAM Role to an EC2 instance allows AWS to automatically rotate and issue temporary security credentials to the instance, eliminating the catastrophic risk of accidentally leaking hardcoded API keys on GitHub.","id":2,"options":["IAM Roles do not support permissions","IAM Roles provide temporary rotating credentials automatically via instance metadata without storing sensitive keys in code or files","IAM Roles are twice as fast as IAM Users","IAM Users cannot connect to S3"],"question":"Why are IAM Roles preferred over hardcoded IAM User Access Keys when granting EC2 instances access to Amazon S3?"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Security Groups are stateful firewalls operating at the instance/ENI level (if inbound traffic is allowed, corresponding outbound response traffic is automatically permitted). NACLs are stateless rules evaluated at the subnet boundary.","id":3,"options":["Security Groups are stateful (inbound traffic response is automatically allowed outbound); NACLs are stateless and operate at the subnet level","Security Groups only work on Windows servers","NACLs are managed by Google Cloud","There is no difference between them"],"question":"What is the primary architectural difference between an AWS Security Group and a Network ACL (NACL)?"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Pre-signed URLs include authentication query parameters generated using the server's IAM credentials, allowing an unauthenticated client to upload or download only the specified object for a strict time window.","id":4,"options":["It permanently changes bucket permissions to public for 5 minutes","It encodes a temporary cryptographic signature using server IAM credentials that grants access only to a specific object key for a limited expiration window","It bypasses Amazon S3 security policies entirely","It requires the user to log in with an AWS root account password"],"question":"How does an S3 Pre-Signed URL allow secure client uploads without making the entire bucket publicly readable/writable?"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Database instances should always reside in private subnets with no public internet routing. Security groups must restrict database access solely to backend application servers located within the authorized VPC.","id":5,"options":["In a public subnet with an open 0.0.0.0/0 security group rule on port 3306","In a private subnet with no public IP address, accessible only by security group rules permitting traffic from the EC2 backend server","Directly on the client user's mobile phone","On an unencrypted FTP server"],"question":"Where should you place your Amazon RDS database instance in a secure VPC architecture?"}],"resources":[{"description":"Free interactive learning courses and cloud architecture pathways.","name":"AWS Skill Builder Official Modules","url":"https://skillbuilder.aws/"},{"description":"Architectural best practices for security, reliability, performance, and cost.","name":"AWS Well-Architected Framework","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/architecture/well-architected/"},{"description":"Complete guide to launching, configuring, and connecting to EC2 instances.","name":"Amazon EC2 Linux User Guide","url":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AWSEC2/latest/UserGuide/"}],"syllabus":[{"code_snippet":"// Least-Privilege IAM Policy for S3 Resume Bucket\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Sid\": \"AllowS3ResumeUploads\",\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\",\n        \"s3:GetObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::careersense-resumes-prod/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","deep_dive":"Never use the AWS root account for daily operations. Create IAM roles with tightly scoped JSON policy permissions and attach them directly to EC2 instances to avoid baking static API keys into code.","key_concepts":["AWS Shared Responsibility Model","IAM Users, Groups & Roles","Least Privilege Principle","Security Groups vs Network ACLs"],"module_title":"Module 1: Cloud Security Fundamentals & IAM"},{"code_snippet":"# NGINX Configuration on EC2 (/etc/nginx/sites-available/careersense)\nserver {\n    listen 80;\n    server_name api.careersense.ai;\n\n    location / {\n        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:5000;\n        proxy_http_version 1.1;\n        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;\n        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';\n        proxy_set_header Host $host;\n        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;\n        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;\n    }\n}","deep_dive":"EC2 provides resizable compute capacity in the cloud. We configure an Ubuntu instance, lock down Security Groups to port 80/443 (HTTP/HTTPS) and port 22 (SSH), and run NGINX to reverse-proxy traffic to backend node processes.","key_concepts":["AMI Selection (Ubuntu 22.04 LTS)","Instance Types (t3.micro / t3.small)","SSH Keypair Authentication","NGINX Reverse Proxy & Certbot Let's Encrypt"],"module_title":"Module 2: Amazon EC2 Compute & Production Host Configuration"},{"code_snippet":"# Generating an S3 Pre-Signed Upload URL in Python (Boto3)\nimport boto3\nfrom botocore.config import Config\n\ns3_client = boto3.client('s3', region_name='us-east-1', config=Config(signature_version='s3v4'))\n\ndef generate_presigned_upload_url(bucket_name, object_key, expires_in=300):\n    url = s3_client.generate_presigned_url(\n        'put_object',\n        Params={'Bucket': bucket_name, 'Key': object_key, 'ContentType': 'application/pdf'},\n        ExpiresIn=expires_in\n    )\n    return url","deep_dive":"Storing user resumes or PDFs on local EC2 disk is brittle (lost when instances terminate). Storing assets in Amazon S3 provides 99.999999999% (11 9s) durability. CloudFront caches assets at edge locations worldwide.","key_concepts":["S3 Buckets & Object Storage","Pre-Signed URLs for Secure Client Uploads","Block Public Access Configuration","CloudFront Low-Latency Edge Caching"],"module_title":"Module 3: Amazon S3 & CloudFront Global CDN"},{"code_snippet":"# Secure Cloud Production Environment Variables (.env)\nDATABASE_URL=mysql+pymysql://careersense_app:SecureRDSSecret@careersense-db.c9k4x.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com:3306/careersense_ai\nAWS_STORAGE_BUCKET_NAME=careersense-resumes-prod\nAWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1\nCDN_DOMAIN=https://d123456abcdef8.cloudfront.net","deep_dive":"Amazon RDS automates hardware provisioning, database setup, patching, and backups. Placing RDS in private VPC subnets ensures database ports (3306) are never directly exposed to the public internet.","key_concepts":["Managed MySQL Instance Provisioning","Multi-AZ Deployments for High Availability","Automated Backups & Point-in-Time Recovery","VPC Private Subnet Security"],"module_title":"Module 4: Amazon RDS Managed Databases & Cloud Architecture"}],"title":"AWS Cloud Architecture & Scalable Deployment","topics":["IAM Roles, Least-Privilege Policies & Security Groups","Amazon EC2 Compute Instances, SSH Keys & NGINX Reverse Proxy","Amazon S3 Object Storage, Bucket Policies & CloudFront CDN","Amazon RDS Managed MySQL Databases & Cloud Production Deployment"]},"duration_weeks":"Week 4 (Sprint)","expected_outcome":"Proficiency in configuring scalable AWS cloud infrastructure, security groups, and automated production deployment.","id":517,"order_index":6,"phase_number":6,"practice_project":"Deploy CareerSense AI Full-Stack Application on AWS EC2 with S3 File Storage & Amazon RDS MySQL","priority":"HIGH","progress":0,"resource_categories":[{"description":"Free interactive learning courses and cloud architecture pat